{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Azchirah</b> — a hint that he would play music at night. Or 'at night I will remember' — that I would play music in ancient days, to serve HaShem, in the manner of 'I will awaken the dawn.'" "<b>And my spirit searched</b> — it is the one who searches, and it is joined to what follows it, namely 'the deeds of Olam' [le'olamim], and the passive participle is deficient [chaser], and it refers to me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:46.458239221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}